Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Stability of fixed points", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9574650962286863`*^9, 3.9574650997562885`*^9}, {
  3.957465260521819*^9, 
  3.9574652669793916`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"cc5d4ddb-8fbe-4d32-9302-\
9aa443d6adf8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "To understand the stability of fixed points, we linearize the beta \
functions around these point.To do that, First we take the first order \
partial derivatives w..rt each parameter, and then bring them together to end \
up at an eigenvalue problem as  d",
 StyleBox["G",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "/dt = ",
 StyleBox["M",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ",
 StyleBox["G, ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "where ",
 StyleBox["G",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " = (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["g", "1"], ",", " ", 
    SubscriptBox["g", "2"]}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "f9abb802-35b1-4620-8d1c-73b3e858a0f7"],
 "), and ",
 StyleBox["M",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " is a 2\[Times]2 matrix. \n Here M is a function of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["g", "1"], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "cc05a060-32ae-45a9-a188-6294a87b989f"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["g", "2"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "f1af95e0-dbb6-49ae-b530-0494b0a2d358"],
 ". To find the stability of a fixed point, we plug in its ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    SubscriptBox["g", 
     RowBox[{"1", "c"}]]}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "be86ebed-ca72-45ab-a75f-ad41a40b765b"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["g", 
    RowBox[{"2", "c"}]], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "1d2b875d-1df8-4b2a-a24a-b7d180f1224e"],
 ") to this matrix and calculate its eigenvalues.\n  If the eigenvalues are \
all negative, the fixed point is stable. If all or some of them are positive, \
then the fixed point is not stable and must be fine-tuned. Number of positive \
eigenvalues give us a measure of stability (zero being most stable), while \
the corresponding eigenvectors tell the direction in which the system must be \
tuned. "
}], "Text",
